Well, this is the typical YAFAP, playing as a Valkyrie and all, but hey, 
gimme a break. :) Did this a week ago and was finally able to find a news 
server that allowed posting, so some of the details are a little sketchy 
from memory (I don't take good notes).

Celes entered the Dungeons of Doom with decent stats, nothing to sneeze at. 
She walked around dlvl 1 with her trusty kitten named Kitty until she found 
a co-aligned altar. After a few sacs, she got bored and decided to start 
decending. Found the stairs to the mines on dlvl2, went down and got the 
usual pickaxe, mithril, iron shoes, dwarfish iron helm, etc. Found a BoT 
lying around on the second level of the mines, so she went back up to dlvl1 
to do some more sac'ing. On the first BoT sac, I believe it was a jackal, 
she got Mjollnir, and 3 sacs later she got Magicbane. She wielded Mr. 
Mjollnir for the rest of the game, though he got a nice drinking buddy 
later on. Anyway, she continued on past minetown (cross-aligned altar and 
nothing of interest in the shops), and found a BoH in a corner of the level 
after minetown. She went to decend another level, and gave her magic 
whistle a toot...only to find that Kitty the large cat was now Kitty the 
lurker above. 'Crap', she thought. Celes went down the stairs with Kitty 
still in tow, and thought 'Crap' again as she turned a corner and saw a 
white dragon coming her way. Feeling a bit suicidal, she decided that she 
could probably take it on although she was explevel 8 with AC:-2. After a 
hundred turns and a lot of the E-word, the dragon went down, no scales 
though. She had realized that she was almost burdened, so she went back to 
minetown to start a stash, dropped a lot of crap, then decided to check the 
shops again. Celes saw a pretty expensive scroll that later on turned out 
to be stinking cloud, and hoped that Kitty the lurker above could steal it 
for her, so she whistled him in...

Kitty swallows Pakka-Pakka. "Burrrrp!" Pakka Pakka is killed!

Kitty's name then got changed to Burpy, and Celes decided to take over 
minetown. :) With all the gold from the shopkeepers (barring Izchak), and a 
few piece of equipment from the minetown guards, everything was looking 
peachy. Celes donated her gold to the priest to get a nice AC, picked up a 
guard's silver sabre, enhanced the skill, and two-weaponed with Mjollnir. 
She kept this combo for the rest of the game, and it was a nice combo at 
that. Her and Burpy, cleared out the rest of the mines for a nice lucky 
trinket, went up to Sokoban and got another BoH out of it, then decided to 
pay The Oracle a visit. "Burrrrp!" :) This was also a bones level from the 
early death of a wizard that I had, so she took his CoMR, and two(!) magic 
markers. Celes found the dungeons a bit boring until the quest level, where 
Burpy stepped on a trap, turned into a paper golem, and got pulverized by a 
few fire after following me through the teleporter. She used Burpy's 
remains for a few Enchant scrolls later on. She was only level 12 when I 
got to the quest, so she went down to pay Medusa a visit, dug down and 
luckily found a ring of levitation on the next level, then went back up and 
watched Medusa get stoned. Cleared out the castle and got some scales from 
a silver dragon 'round the back, sat on the throne and genocided master 
mind flayers, got the WoW at 0:3 and padded out my AK. Blessed scroll of 
charging, Tshirt, GoP, HoT, speed boots, and another blessed magic marker.
Went back up to the minetown stash to drop a few things, then went to The 
late Oracle's abode to blank useless scrolls and enchant the AK. When she 
was done, she had Mjollnir and a silver sabre at +7, all her armour at +4, 
and a very sore wrist from writing all those scrolls. While enchanting, she 
accidentally vaporized her GoP, so the wrested WoW gave her another pair. 
After all the castle enemies and a potion of gain level, she was ready for 
the quest. Lord Surtur went down in two hits, and Celes took the Orb of 
Cheapness and the Bell of Opening. Not much was to be said about Gehennom, 
other than it was boring as hell (hooray for bad puns). Celes shocked & 
slashed all the demon lords that bothered her, killed Vlad in one hit, 
found the VS, marked it, then went to go make friends with a certain 
wizard. She didn't bother with Orcus' WoD during the game, shock&slash was 
fun enough. She went down to the VS to relax by putting on a little mood 
light, playing some soothing music, and reading a nice book, though she was 
a little shocked when the dungeon around her started to crumble. The 
sanctum was cake with all of her equipment, only got hit by the mysterious 
force 3 or 4 times, all only one level or better. She went back up to 
dlvl1, checked that she had everything needed, and went up the stairs 
expecting to see the Dodge Caravan that she had parked outside quite a 
while ago, but instead ended up on the plane of earth. Elvenking, Rodney, 
and the minotaur all went down quickly, then she dug to the portal. She 
didn't bother with the air elementals on the plane of air, instead 
teleporting them with a few trusty wands every time she was engulfed. Celes 
had some trouble finding the portal on the plane of fire, but all was well 
when she stepped on it while battling 8 monsters at once. The plane of 
water was boring, took a while for her to find the portal though. On the 
astral plane, she donned her towel and saw that Famine was on the left. She 
downed a meal and headed for him, not even getting attacked by him once. 
Checked the altar and luckily it was Odin's.

